#!/bin/sh

# The release must not start distribution itself: OtpDebugMcp.Target starts
# it at connect time as a hidden node, in the name mode the target uses.
export RELEASE_DISTRIBUTION=none

# --help and --version, answered here, before the release script's own
# commands and without starting the VM.
case "${RELEASE_COMMAND:-}" in
  --help | -h | help)
    cat <<EOF
otp_debug_mcp <%= @release.version %>: an MCP server that lets an AI agent debug a running
Erlang/Elixir/OTP node. It attaches over distribution as a hidden node, so the
node needs no changes, and starts every investigation with diagnose.

Usage:
  $RELEASE_PROG start        Run the server, speaking MCP over stdin and stdout.
                             An MCP client launches it this way; you don't.
  $RELEASE_PROG --version    Print the version.
  $RELEASE_PROG --help       Print this.

Register it with Claude Code, for all projects:
  claude mcp add otp-debug --scope user -- $RELEASE_ROOT/bin/$RELEASE_PROG start
Then ask, e.g.: "myapp@myhost is getting slower. Find out why."
Or start from one of its prompts, in Claude Code's / menu:
  /mcp__otp-debug__help                       what it can do, with examples
  /mcp__otp-debug__investigate NODE SYMPTOM   find out what's wrong
  /mcp__otp-debug__watch NODE MINUTES         wait for a problem, then dig in

What it can do, and the tools for it (the agent picks them; you describe the
problem):
<%= OtpDebugMcp.Capabilities.text() %>

Settings, environment variables of the server (claude mcp add -e NAME=VALUE):
  OTP_DEBUG_MCP_COOKIE      The Erlang cookie for connect, so it stays out of
                            the conversation. Default: the cookie given to
                            connect, else ~/.erlang.cookie.
  OTP_DEBUG_MCP_CONFIRM     Ask the user before each step: all, changes (only
                            the steps that change something on the node), or
                            off. Default: off. load_module always asks.
  OTP_DEBUG_MCP_READ_ONLY   true: refuse every step that would change something
                            on the node (tracing, forced garbage collection,
                            the recorder, remote_eval, load_module...).
                            Default: false.
  OTP_DEBUG_MCP_AUDIT_LOG   The file every tool call is recorded in, one JSON
                            line each, or off. Default:
                            ~/.local/state/otp_debug_mcp/audit.jsonl
  OTP_DEBUG_MCP_ALLOW_EVAL  true: enable remote_eval, arbitrary code on the
                            node. Default: false.

Also in this release's bin: otp-debug-k8s, which runs the server as a pod next
to an app in Kubernetes (otp-debug-k8s --help).

Documentation: https://github.com/ayarodionov/otp_debug_mcp
(and README.md, docs/ and skills/ next to bin/ in a downloaded release)
EOF
    exit 0
    ;;
  --version | -v)
    echo "otp_debug_mcp <%= @release.version %>"
    exit 0
    ;;
esac
